            <ArticleTitle>Rectal inflammation as first manifestation of graft-vs-host disease: radiologic-pathologic findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>L75-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Graft-vs-host disease (GVHD) is a common, life-threatening complication of bone marrow transplantation that frequently involves the gastrointestinal tract. Since symptoms are typically nonspecific, radiologic examination is often performed to reach a diagnosis. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first reported radiologic description of a case of rectal involvement as the first manifestation of GVHD. The differential diagnosis of segmental rectal wall thickening in a patient following bone marrow transplantation should include GVHD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
